1. Child Process - fork(): used to create a new Child Process. Parent and child run independently, where child get a copy of the parent process.

2. Signals : they are software interrupts send to process to notify events.

3. Kernel crashes: happens becoz of driver bugs, null pointer deference, invalid memory access.

4. Time Complexity: way to describe how much time an algo takes to execute based on the size of inputs.

5. Locking mechanism: a technique used to avoid race condition in multi-threading.
 5.1. mutex: helps single thread to enter into critical section at a time
 5.2. spin lock: a thread run continuously checking lock, without sleep
